w scissors $$$b_2$$$ times and show paper $$$b_3$$$ times. Though, both Alice and Bob did not choose the sequence in which they show things. It is guaranteed that $$$a_1 + a_2 + a_3 = n$$$ and $$$b_1 + b_2 + b_3 = n$$$.Your task is to find two numbers:  the minimum number of round Alice can win;  the maximum number of rounds Alice can win. \n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Python 3 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nn=int(input())\na=list(map(int,input().rstrip().split()))\nb=list(map(int,input().rstrip().split()))\na1,a2,a3=a[0],a[1],a[2]\nb1,b2,b3=b[0],b[1],b[2]\nans=[0,0]\nans[1]=min(a1,b2)+min(a2,b3)+min(a3,b1)\nans[0]=max(0,b1-a1-a2,b2-a2-a3,b3-a1-a3)\nprint(*ans)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0.5, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().rstrip().split()))\nb = list(map(int, input().rstrip().split()))\na1, a2, a3 = a[0], a[1], a[2]\nb1, b2, b3 = b[0], b[1], b[2]\n\n# Maximum wins for Alice:\n# Alice wins when:\n#   Alice rock (a1) beats Bob scissors (b2)\n#   Alice scissors (a2) beats Bob paper (b3)\n#   Alice paper (a3) beats Bob rock (b1)\nmax_wins = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n\n# Minimum wins for Alice:\n# We want to minimize Alice's wins, which means maximizing:\n# - Draws (same moves)\n# - Bob's wins (Alice loses)\n# Total rounds = n\n# Alice wins + Bob wins + draws = n\n# So minimum Alice wins = n - (max possible draws + max possible Bob wins)\n\n# For Bob's wins:\n# Bob wins when:\n#   Bob rock (b1) beats Alice scissors (a2)\n#   Bob scissors (b2) beats Alice paper (a3)\n#   Bob paper (b3) beats Alice rock (a1)\n# So max Bob wins = min(b1, a2) + min(b2, a3) + min(b3, a1)\n\n# Max draws = min(a1, b1) + min(a2, b2) + min(a3, b3)\n\nmax_draws_and_bob_wins = min(a1, b1) + min(a2, b2) + min(a3, b3) + min(b1, a2) + min(b2, a3) + min(b3, a1)\nmin_wins = max(0, n - max_draws_and_bob_wins)\n\nprint(min_wins, max_wins)\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.152555099310121e-07, -5.1616290875244886e-05, -4.172316494077677e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.005299804266542196, -0.14268852770328522, -4.172316494077677e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0024802894331514835, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.00026663561584427953, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.629365427419543e-06, -4.362964682513848e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.009987853467464447, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576272320060525e-06, -5.125986263010418e-06, -6.556489552167477e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.71926071238704e-05, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -7.629365427419543e-06, -5.602820692729438e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.0019350391812622547, -4.6491513785440475e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.643566590966657e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -6.556489552167477e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.0649541915627196e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -7.152531907195225e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, -6.079655122448457e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00010954733443213627, -1.1920858014491387e-05, -2.253030106658116e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -0.005935542285442352, -7.199982064776123e-05, -0.03358721360564232, -0.011894021183252335, -0.12750768661499023, -1.0490362910786644e-05, -0.1365000158548355, -5.5549986427649856e-05, -0